1.4.7
    - New normalization bandpasses from STScI's public TRDS library:
       * 2MASS J H Ks
       * Cousins R I
       * Gaia G Gbp GRp
       * Galex NUV (FUV already existed)
       * Johnson U B R I J K (V already existed)
       * Landolt U B V R I
       * SDSS u g r i z
       * Spitzer irac,3_6um irac,4_5um irac,5_8um irac,8_0um mips,24um
       * Stromgren u v b y
       * WISE W1 W2 W3 W4
    - Replaced default spectra of GD71 and GD153 with new TRDS
      spectra that cover a broader wavelength range
    - Added three new HLSP spectra for O2V, O4V, O5V courtesy of 
      Leonardo Ubeda
    - Warnings squashed
    - UV MOS Imager recognized as an imaging channel again

1.4.6
    - Completely rewritten thermal emission handler, uses the OTA
      temperature for now instead of the detector temperature.
    - Instrument.set_from_hwome() loader now trims spectra of any
      red/blue leaks (redundant with recent versions of hwome_data)
    - Telescope.set_from_hwome() can now accept a preconfigured 
      DataModel, rather than just an EAC name.
    - IFS and MOS are now their own Instrument classes again, both 
      subclasses of MultiSpec. They still operate on "disperser"
      elements.
    - MultiSpec still exists independently for anyone who switched 
      their API usage, it will trigger a DeprecationWarning.
    - You can now set SourceExposure.extraction_aperture in units of 
      arcseconds. In the camera, it's the radius of the extraction 
      aperture. If it's a spectrograph or IFS, it's the half-height
      of the extraction box. If it's a MOS, it's ignored in favor
      of the microshutter size. If unset, None, or 0, it defaults 
      to the previous aperture behavior.
    - The number of iterations in SourceExposure_do_update_magnitude
      has been decreased from 15 to 12, in the hopes of not 
      triggering the recursion threshold for some users.
    - Several docstrings
    - The new FUV_MOS echelle is NOT working yet.
1.4.5
    - Fixed a bug in SourceExposure._do_update_magnitude() that stopped 
      calcs-for-magnitude from actually running
    - Fixed a bug in SourceMultiSpecExposure.calculate_exptime() that
      stopped calcs-for-exptime from running
    - Updated the wrappers to use the new 
      Telescope.find_instrument_with() API
    - Zodi background generation has been moved to its own file
    - Profile generation has been moved to its own file and class
    - Telescope.save_to_dict() and Instrument.save_to_dict() now contain
      the hwome-core version and hwome_data commit as well
1.4.4
    - IFS Instrument is renamed MultiSpec
    - UV MOS and UV IFS are now BOTH MultiSpec instruments
    - The type appended to the instrument name for UV MOS is now "MOS",
      not "Spectrograph".
    - The special "ifs" band type is no more, they are "disperser" now.
      In its place, Telescope.find_instrument_with() now allows a search
      for "instrument" (using a string that contains at least a fragment of
      the name, e.g. "MOS")
    - Bug fix: The extraction box sizes in 1.4.3 were both actually the
      Spectroscopy aperture (3x the PSF FWHM height by 2 pixel width).
      These have now been corrected to actually use the MOS slitlet size
      or the width of the IFU slicer.
    - Bug fix: The SourceExposure.wave object now parallels the construction
      of the SNR, exptime, or magnitude outputs. Previously, in a multi-band 
      (or multi-source, for what is now MultiSpec) situation, the wavelength
      array was not necessarily matched to the SNR or exptime array and
      attempting to plot the result might fail.
1.4.3
    - New extended source support, paralleling the JWST Pandeia Engine
    - Sources have an additional parameter, geometry; format is the same
      as the JWST ETC's Pandeia Engine
    - New dependency on `photutils`
    - Now reads the MOS slitlet config and IFS Image Slicer config to get
      aperture widths for slitlets and IFS.
    - New computation of flux within aperture using 2D profiles and 
      2D aperture masks
    - Thermal, dark, and zodi contributions now correspond to the 2D 
      aperture mask dimensions
    - configuration["band"] is now configuration["bands"] but you should
      use instrument.bands anyway.
    - mirror area is now the real area; for EAC5 that means hexagons with
      gaps. Diameter is now the effective diameter.
    - solving for magnitude works again (to ~0.1 magnitude accuracy), with
      some performance cost
    - improved find_instrument_with can also search for specific wavelength
      coverage, a specific wavelength band, or resolving power (either
      greater-than-x, or a range)
1.4.2
    - Fix SNR bug
    - New Zodi function from pyEDITH
    - Source objects now have RA and Dec
1.4.1
    - Save-to-dict functionality now writes software version
    - Fixed spectrograph fringing and G120M/G180M functionality
    - Running calculate_exptime() (or the others) no longer accidentally
      sets the Instrument.band permanently.
1.4.0
    - Data from HWOME
    - Calculation functions standardized and genericized
    - Telescope now automatically loads all instruments
    - All optical elements are now "bands"
    - All functions now return a single band's exptime, snr, or magnitude
